X------------------------------------------------------------------------------
XIDENTIFYING RINGS:
X
XTo figure out what a ring is, again start by figuring out if the ring is 
Xcursed or not.  If the ring is cursed, don't throw it away!  It's a prime 
Xcandidate for identification through the first method:  chuck it down a sink, 
Xand see what happens.  See the SINK EFFECTS section for more information about 
Xwhat happens when various ring types are thrown down a sink.  If the ring 
Xisn't cursed, it probably is somewhat beneficial.  Try it on.  If something 
Xhappens immediately, you'll know what it is (levitation, for example).  Some 
Xrings can only be identified after being worn for a while - for example, a 
Xring of polymorph will only polymorph you every once in a while, and a ring of 
Xteleport also only works now and then.  Other rings can only be guessed at - 
Xfor instance, if you suddenly can find secret doors easier than you have been, 
Xit might be a ring of searching.  If you suddenly are killing monsters more 
Xeasily, it might be a ring of increase damage. 
